---
title: The Wriggling Man
tags: []
date: 2025-02-24T00:00:00-04:00
campaigns: [deep-eyes]
---

The Wriggling Man stands in the garden of the [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/index|Gilded Spire]], seen through the [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Rhett]]. He was a person, and the magic that tore the garden cut him into rows and set them off kilter: the pieces move and will not hold, and pushed together they would make a man again. He wears old chrome, more primitive than what is worn on Syrin now, one prosthetic arm with its metal connection left showing. The magic about him feels stagnant, and he has stood there a few centuries at least.

He is a fact of the place. So long as the garden stands it is simply true that he exists there, and killing him frees him only until he draws himself back together, in a day or so. The same shattering took the people of [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/Della Caldera|Della Caldera]] when the town's aeternalis went up. None of the person he was survives to be read, and once his body is let go he cannot be touched or carried off.
